{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l1nxc4yu","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 2 Offline","year":2013,"examDate":2013,"subject":"physics","chapter":"heat-and-thermodynamics","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"specific-heat-capacity-calorimetry-and-change-of-state","type":"mcqm","marks":4,"negMarks":2,"permalink":"pthe-figure-below-shows-the-variation-of-specific-heat-cap-jee-advanced-physics-units-and-measurements-69s1bxduuzcbhors","content":"<p>The figure below shows the variation of specific heat capacity (C) of a solid as a function of temperature (T). The temperature is increased continuously from 0 to 500 K at a constant rate. Ignoring any volume change, the following statement(s) is(are) correct to a reasonable approximation.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1qh6sg7/4931062f-9775-4789-90bb-4015e8af7354/6e3fb970-b741-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qh6sg8.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l1qh6sg7/4931062f-9775-4789-90bb-4015e8af7354/6e3fb970-b741-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qh6sg8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Heat and Thermodynamics Question 38 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l1qh6sg7/4931062f-9775-4789-90bb-4015e8af7354/6e3fb970-b741-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qh6sg8.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l1qh6sg7/4931062f-9775-4789-90bb-4015e8af7354/6e3fb970-b741-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qh6sg8.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1qh6sg7/4931062f-9775-4789-90bb-4015e8af7354/6e3fb970-b741-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qh6sg8.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l1qh6sg7/4931062f-9775-4789-90bb-4015e8af7354/6e3fb970-b741-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qh6sg8.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l1qh6sg7/4931062f-9775-4789-90bb-4015e8af7354/6e3fb970-b741-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qh6sg8.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l1qh6sg7/4931062f-9775-4789-90bb-4015e8af7354/6e3fb970-b741-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qh6sg8.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"The rate at which heat is absorbed in the range 0-100 K varies linearly with temperature T."},{"identifier":"B","content":"Heat absorbed in increasing the temperature from 0-100 K is less than the heat required for increasing the temperature from 400-500 K."},{"identifier":"C","content":"There is no change in the rate of heat absorption in the range 400-500 K."},{"identifier":"D","content":"The rate of heat absorption increases in the range 200-300 K."}],"correct_options":["A","B","C","D"],"explanation":"<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1qh998r/942416f6-c799-4a0b-975e-6ff52cdf3d02/b2d714c0-b741-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qh998s.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l1qh998r/942416f6-c799-4a0b-975e-6ff52cdf3d02/b2d714c0-b741-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qh998s.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Heat and Thermodynamics Question 38 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l1qh998r/942416f6-c799-4a0b-975e-6ff52cdf3d02/b2d714c0-b741-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qh998s.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l1qh998r/942416f6-c799-4a0b-975e-6ff52cdf3d02/b2d714c0-b741-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qh998s.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1qh998r/942416f6-c799-4a0b-975e-6ff52cdf3d02/b2d714c0-b741-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qh998s