436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(760,0)\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1593,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>= m area under C-T curve</p>\n<p>From the graph it is clear that area under C-T is more in 400-500 K than in 0-100 K.</p>\n<p>Therefore, heat absorbed in 0-100 K is less than in 400-500 K.</p>\n<p>(c) In 400-500 K,</p>\n<p>C remains constant so there is no change in R.</p>\n<p>(d) In 200-300 K,</p>\n<p>C increases so R increases.</p>"}]}